WEBVTT

00:37:29.393 --> 00:37:32.432
And in the last few years,
I've just had to turn off Twitter,

00:37:32.456 --> 00:37:35.379
because I don't want to see
what you like on social media."

00:37:35.403 --> 00:37:38.442
She does not want to know
their opinions on immigration policy.

00:37:38.466 --> 00:37:40.559
She just wants to know them
as human beings.

00:37:40.583 --> 00:37:42.302
And as human beings, they get along.

00:37:42.326 --> 00:37:45.465
When they start talking
about Donald Trump, they get into trouble.

00:37:45.489 --> 00:37:47.522
So they try not to talk about it.

00:37:48.364 --> 00:37:49.711
CA: But it still seems to me

00:37:49.735 --> 00:37:55.375
that there's an art to how communities
can embrace and bring in outsiders,

00:37:55.399 --> 00:37:58.186
and that there's a huge difference
between that feeling of,

00:37:58.210 --> 00:38:02.053
"People are coming in on our terms
and welcomed by us,"